          "options": {
            "content": "**Purpose** \u2014 decide whether the policy service nodes are coping, and which one is not.\n\n**Read it in this order**\n\n1. Read busiest load and worst latency. Both green means the PSNs are not the problem \u2014 go back to RADIUS access.\n2. Find the outlier node in the utilisation panels.\n3. Confirm it in the diagnostic work queue and the connection-state timeline.\n\n**When something is red**\n\n- Saturation with errors: a capacity problem \u2014 rebalance or add a node.\n- Errors without saturation: certificates, the identity store, or policy \u2014 continue on RADIUS access.\n- Suppression climbing: ISE is dropping logs, so treat the reporting panels on every dashboard as incomplete until it recovers.\n\n**Related dashboards** \u2014 Triage, RADIUS access, Control plane, Collection pipeline\n\n*Owner: set this to the team that answers the page. Runbook: link it here \u2014 a red panel with no runbook is a puzzle, not an alert.*",
